{"id": "EUVD-2026-55824", "enisaUuid": "ad810a65-e7cd-3303-ad00-019f6f370605", "description": "A flaw was found in the Data Science Pipelines Operator. This vulnerability allows an unauthenticated attacker to derive sensitive credentials, such as MariaDB root/user passwords and MinIO access/secret keys, if they can access the MinIO Route or MariaDB Service. The flaw occurs because the operator uses a cryptographically weak pseudo-random number generator (PRNG) to generate these credentials, making them predictable. Successful exploitation could lead to unauthorized access to all pipeline artifacts and metadata, resulting in significant information disclosure.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T20:45:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-21T11:27:13", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:53261", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:53262", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:53263", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:60367", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:60520", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:65126", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-18611", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2510299"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5qmg-pgg7-3rjj", "CVE-2026-18611"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.61, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "100c3ca6-4461-32da-8790-7d645c144a2d", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift AI 3.4", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1784833428"}, {"id": "6c4812eb-64c8-392c-97e8-ded3314d730a", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift AI 3.5", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1786552250"}, {"id": "6cd51a75-efda-3232-bb23-f5f64459ca50", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift AI 3.4", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1787002057"}, {"id": "82943165-8b96-322e-bafd-f2c5f1ec092c", "product": {"name": "Red Hat OpenShift A